// Japan map polygons: GEO (shared across works).
// Keys "18"-"46" were extracted verbatim from legacy/index.html (JIS prefecture codes,
// named after the old provinces). That data ends at Shinano/Totomi, which left the Kanto
// region sea-colored and Japan looking cut off east of Shizuoka. The Kanto entries "8"-"14"
// and "19" (Kai, Sagami, Musashi x2, Kozuke, Shimotsuke, Hitachi, Shimosa) are now REAL
// coastlines: their mainland outer rings come from real JIS prefecture boundaries
// (dataofjapan/land, projection-compatible with the legacy pixels) projected through GEO.proj
// and Douglas-Peucker-simplified to the legacy fidelity — see scripts/build-kanto-geo.mjs.
// (An earlier hand-drawn version read as fake in a family playtest — observation memo 2026-07-14.)
// The three prefectures that hold more than one old province are keyed by PROVINCE SLUG instead
// of a JIS code — owari/mikawa (愛知), totomi/suruga/izu (静岡), shimosa/kazusa/awa (千葉) — because
// a shape named 尾張 that also covers 三河 makes any coloring of it a false claim (WRITING 地図書法2).
// They are the exact union of their municipalities; see scripts/build-province-geo.mjs.
// A pref id is therefore an opaque string, not a number: engine code compares ids as strings.
// This file is therefore hand-managed; the verbatim-extraction pipeline it once came from
// has been retired (same policy as faces/story/map).
// Projection: x=(lon-proj.lonmin)*proj.s*proj.k, y=(proj.latmax-lat)*proj.s.
// The added land intentionally extends past vb (x>1000): it fills the frame edge in wide views.
// vb itself is no longer a frame — it is only the display reference (panel aspect + on-screen
// scale) — because both map frames are now content-fit and derived per work: campaignViewBox
// (notebook map) and locatorWindow (scene-map「いま ここ」mini-map). Land past a frame is clipped
// by it, so the country reads as running off the edge rather than being cut.
/* eslint-disable */

import type { Geo } from '../engine/types';

